  body: |
    # Relevant week for ESA part-week payments

    ## Authored interpretation

    The source bases a part-week payment on notional entitlement for a relevant week that depends on whether the payment arises at the beginning, end or change of benefit week.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 46043 points to separate definitions at 46052, 46082 and 46103. The relevant week cannot be assumed to be the current calendar week; no part-week award is calculated.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 46043, PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e5ffc3de262afd82fcf92b/dmg-Chap-46.pdf#page=9)

    ## Evidence and review status

    This is an unreviewed, model-assisted interpretation of selected passages in the frozen DWP guidance. It is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule. ESA(Cont), ESA(IR), New Style ESA, UC and Pension Credit are not equated. The captured source contains historical, transitional and potentially superseded provisions; no complete or current legal rule set is claimed. Machine extraction can affect reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF review or specialist acceptance is claimed.

    Source captured: 2026-09-15T19:45:29.420524Z. This is an acquisition time, not a publication, revision or commencement date. Source-stated dates retain their own role and precision.

